title Six of eight carry the fields
prompt Keaton -- rebuild rishi on all seven peer trees
think Every peer has a live loop, so a write into its tree is a write beside another writer. I touched only the gitignored binary and no git state at all, and proved that afterward rather than claiming it.
think A binary that is EXECUTING cannot be written -- the linker refuses with ETXTBSY -- so each build went to a temp name and was renamed over. A rename is atomic and a running process keeps its old inode, so a peer mid-lap kept the interpreter it started with.
obs I CHECKED THE SOURCE BEFORE BUILDING, which is what kept two rebuilds from being lies. copal and grass have not pulled the change, so building there would have remade the OLD interpreter and left a fresh timestamp saying otherwise.
obs DIFFUSER HAD ALREADY REBUILT ITSELF at 21:52, before I arrived. Its own lap met the rostered guard, read the refusal, and did the work -- which is the mechanism proving itself without a hand.
obs Rebuilt four -- bakery, patchouli, petrichor, pheromone -- and PROVED each by probe rather than by exit code, asserting the interpreter composes a bounded field rather than the literal placeholder. Six of eight carry the fields now.
obs THE TWO LEFT ARE NOT A GAP, they are the path. Their round-open pulls the source and the rishi_brief guard reds and names the rebuild, so the fleet closes itself. Pulling for them would be a git write in a tree that already answers to another writer.
obs A READING I NEARLY TRUSTED WAS STALE. Their behind count read zero against their own xy/main ref, which is only as fresh as their last fetch; comparing their HEAD against mine directly showed copal sitting on my stamp-correction commit and grass earlier still.
obs Confirmed no stray temp binary in any tree and no tracked change of mine anywhere. The tracked changes those trees carry are their own laps in flight.
loom rebuild trees_total=8 carried_before=2 rebuilt_by_hand=4 self_rebuilt=1 pending_pull=2 carried_after=6
loom safety stray_temp_files=0 my_tracked_changes_in_peers=0 method=build_temp_then_rename
rota none -- a fleet-wide rebuild on Keaton's word, no rota this lap
file none in the field; the work was four gitignored interpreters in peer trees
scope four peer interpreters rebuilt and proven by probe, two left to their own pull, one had already done it
status GREEN -- six of eight trees compose bounded fields; the two remaining are behind on source and their guard will name the rebuild
recommend check in (Keaton) -- copal and grass close themselves at their next round-open; nothing here needs a hand
